- You’re building a comment section for a blog.
- Each time a user clicks the “Post” button, you want to show their comment on the page.
- A teammate suggests the following code:
```js
const postBtn = document.getElementById("postBtn");
const commentBox = document.getElementById("commentBox");
const commentSection = document.getElementById("commentSection");

postBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
 const comment = commentBox.value.trim();
 const newComment = document.createElement("p");
 newComment.textContent = comment;
 commentSection.innerHTML += newComment;
});
```
After running this, the browser throws no errors - but the comments don’t show up correctly.

